blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T13:17:36-08:00","id":1016705,"title":"","content":"A lot of those Devotions doesn't specify their Covenant.<br /> <br /> Which Devotions belong to which Covenant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T13:25:59-08:00","id":1016709,"title":"","content":"It was included in the form of a pastebin.<br /> <br /> Also. All of the EricaTeachesNYC ones are Carthian and all of the other ones are Invictus","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T13:37:27-08:00","id":1016714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1016594#post1016594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question for STs. Would you allow a player to take Rapidity for Hekireki?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was about to allow it, but then I reread Hekireki, and this is my answer:<br /> <br /> No, because Hekireki says: She cannot use Vitae during this turn for any purpose. To me that means that you're not supposed to spend it for other effects before activating this either, thus making it impossible to have Rapidity infront.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T13:45:10-08:00","id":1016717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1016679#post1016679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a lot of mechanics I wish would have just been included in some form</div> </div> </div> </div>The plan had been for them to be &quot;included&quot; in the form of hidden references to the pastebin links in the fiction. Unfortunately there wasn't enough space for said hidden references. But here it is all the same. All of this is canon material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-13-2016, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T14:03:58-08:00","id":1016723,"title":"","content":"Seems like another good reason to have Kickstarters for the second edition books, so we potentially won't have as much size limitations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T16:20:28-08:00","id":1016796,"title":"","content":"Word count limits are a terrible thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:05:41-08:00","id":1016815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1016717#post1016717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The plan had been for them to be &quot;included&quot; in the form of hidden references to the pastebin links in the fiction. Unfortunately there wasn't enough space for said hidden references. But here it is all the same. All of this is canon material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Basically, there were a couple of &quot;classified ads&quot; that had to be cut for space. They were little ad blocks, the way you might imagine a zine in the 1980s. One was a defected Invictus knight offering bodyguard services. You could email her at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#563d383f313e22353e333a2533372439393d16313b373f3a7835393b\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"096267606e617d6a616c657a6c687b666662496e64686065276a6664\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>. <br /> <br /> The other was a Carthian offering any member of the Movement in good standing tutelage in some of the Devotions she'd accumulated over the years. She listed her Twitter account, which was ericateachesnyc. She's Daeva; that's why they skew so heavily toward Majesty. <br /> <br /> This wasn't really as much a word count limit thing; I wrote almost all of those well after I turned in final drafts for this book. These paste bins were kind of scrap notebooks for ideas I had here and there. I talked to Rose, she'll be putting them on the resources link once I get them all compiled into the right format, which means getting off my lazy ass and doing it (also, you know, finding a lull in other work). I might integrate some notes people have given me, although I won't do that as rigorously as a standard errata pass, for obvious reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:48:11-08:00","id":1016837,"title":"","content":"minor Criticism? Do you or anyone involved in this project know Hiragana? I do.<br /> <br /> in hekireki the jappanese name has the hiragana <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Consolas\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u306e in it.<br /> <br /> corresponds to the sound 'no'<br /> <br /> but theirs no trace of it in the romanized name.<br /> <br /> Any answers? </span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T18:11:16-08:00","id":1016845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1016837#post1016837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">minor Criticism? Do you or anyone involved in this project know Hiragana? I do.<br /> <br /> in hekireki the jappanese name has the hiragana <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Consolas\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u306e in it.<br /> <br /> corresponds to the sound 'no'<br /> <br /> but theirs no trace of it in the romanized name.<br /> <br /> Any answers? </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The kanji don't match either, it is not the name. It's more a separate epithet that also describes the effect of the power. Rather poetically actually.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, David lives in Tokyo, and while I don't know if it's been confirmed he knows Japanese I am 100% certain that he knows enough not to make that error.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":". 12-13-2016, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T19:11:26-08:00","id":1016867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1016837#post1016837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">minor Criticism? Do you or anyone involved in this project know Hiragana? I do.<br /> <br /> in hekireki the jappanese name has the hiragana <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Consolas\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u306e in it.<br /> <br /> corresponds to the sound 'no'<br /> <br /> but theirs no trace of it in the romanized name.<br /> <br /> Any answers? </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>As answered above, that's not the name.<br /> <br /> It's part of the description, for those curious. That basically means &quot;a feather's flight.&quot; It's pronounced &quot;hane no hisho.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u9739\u9742 is the Japanese name for the power. That romanizes as hekireki. It just means &quot;thunderclap.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'll fuss the description a little to make it clearer. I didn't remember adding that to the description. There was actually a short poem I was writing that was going to be in the description, since as you'll find on Erica's Twitter account, the story was that the author of the letter in the Carthian chapter of Secrets of the Covenants sent her the info about that Devotion. It was posed as a gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 12-13-2016, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T19:28:01-08:00","id":1016870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1016867#post1016867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll fuss the description a little to make it clearer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spacing and italics would probably do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T21:08:48-08:00","id":1016900,"title":"","content":"Completely irrelevant media reference and language tirade ahead: <br /> <br /> Ironically, anyone that's seen Samurai Champloo might recall an episode where Fuu is trying to teach Mugen to read and write in Japanese. About half way through the episode, there's a bit where he's asked to read a block of text. He calls out the no kana (\u306e), recognizing it. He notes it a few more times in the text. <br /> <br /> \u306e is one of the single most common kana you'll see in a piece of Japanese writing, because it denotes possessives. It's essentially the same as adding apostrophe-s to the end of a word. So in this case, the bit I had in that description was <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u7fbd\u306e\u98db\u7fd4. \u7fbd literally means feather, and \u98db\u7fd4 means flight. So, it's basically a feather's flight. And if you're romanizing it, it's literally Whatever-No. Or in this case, hane-no-hisho (pronounced like hah nay no he show basically.) </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mugen knew that particular kana because it's used pretty constantly. I was briefly tickled when that kana was called out there.</span></span><br /> <br /> So if anyone's interested in strangely obscure cross-language reference humor, there you go!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T08:02:44-08:00","id":1017067,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone for their feedback on the Devotions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Some great stuff in there, together with the many devotions of the 2nd ed corebook it goes a long way to adding diversity to the Vampire power set, which was one of my only gripes with core 1st ed.<br /> <br /> Now if we can find space for some bloodlines somewhere in future books, that would be super awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T09:54:52-08:00","id":1017118,"title":"","content":"So, a lot of Carthian devotions are focused on combat. This begs the question of whether or not it changes the first order optimal strategy for building someone combat-y. It may open up rushing high Celerity as being viable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 12-14-2016, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:46:43-08:00","id":1017192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1017118#post1017118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a lot of Carthian devotions are focused on combat. This begs the question of whether or not it changes the first order optimal strategy for building someone combat-y. It may open up rushing high Celerity as being viable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Daeva Carthian was always the best combination for combat characters in 1e. With two physical Disciplines at in-Clan costs and access to a huge host of combat-related Devotions, they were the obvious choice. This is just bringing 2e back up to speed in that department. Only now physical Disciplines are way better and Majesty ties into a lot of the Carthian Devotions. If my friends back in Washington still play Requiem and made the jump to second edition, I bet Mike is drooling over these.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T12:31:55-08:00","id":1017211,"title":"","content":"So... does In Vitae Veritas ignore the requirements of having adjacent targets mesmerized or awed first? And if no, assuming a Ventrue has 21 or 22 vitae to blow, who gets their memories rewritten or possessed, the person in front of them, the adjacent target(s) or both/all targets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T12:52:28-08:00","id":1017230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1016900#post1016900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Completely irrelevant media reference and language tirade ahead:<br /> <br /> Ironically, anyone that's seen Samurai Champloo might recall an episode where Fuu is trying to teach Mugen to read and write in Japanese. About half way through the episode, there's a bit where he's asked to read a block of text. He calls out the no kana (\u306e), recognizing it. He notes it a few more times in the text.<br /> <br /> \u306e is one of the single most common kana you'll see in a piece of Japanese writing, because it denotes possessives. It's essentially the same as adding apostrophe-s to the end of a word. So in this case, the bit I had in that description was <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u7fbd\u306e\u98db\u7fd4. \u7fbd literally means feather, and \u98db\u7fd4 means flight. So, it's basically a feather's flight. And if you're romanizing it, it's literally Whatever-No. Or in this case, hane-no-hisho (pronounced like hah nay no he show basically.) </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mugen knew that particular kana because it's used pretty constantly. I was briefly tickled when that kana was called out there.</span></span><br /> <br /> So if anyone's interested in strangely obscure cross-language reference humor, there you go!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Glad theirs other people studying the language on the Forum.<br /> <br /> Machine, can you tell me where I can get the dark ages vampire badge, just figured out I can download someone elses badge ad add it... but cant find the Vampire dark ages, or Beast badges...<br /> <br /> dont qualify for the other vampire badges, or hunters hunted or demon the descent.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T15:46:43-08:00","id":1017362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1017230#post1017230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Glad theirs other people studying the language on the Forum.<br /> <br /> Machine, can you tell me where I can get the dark ages vampire badge, just figured out I can download someone elses badge ad add it... but cant find the Vampire dark ages, or Beast badges...<br /> <br /> dont qualify for the other vampire badges, or hunters hunted or demon the descent.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea about any of that stuff honestly. I imagine you can contact a forum administrator, maybe with the Contact Us link? But that's so far out my wheelhouse. Maybe <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> can advise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T16:19:51-08:00","id":1017379,"title":"","content":"I don't really know anything about backer badges either. I didn't even think they were an official Thing Onyx Path Does, just assumed they were fan-made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T17:34:24-08:00","id":1017397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1017379#post1017379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really know anything about backer badges either. I didn't even think they were an official Thing Onyx Path Does, just assumed they were fan-made.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one I use for Beast is. I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> made it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T18:01:30-08:00","id":1017413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1016815#post1016815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might integrate some notes people have given me, although I won't do that as rigorously as a standard errata pass, for obvious reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are taking feedback into consideration, I have a thought about Manic Depression. The Manic Condition's Resolution criteria says &quot;When your character fails any action, she stumbles from exhaustion. Resolve this Condition. For the remainder of the scene, all actions are taken at -5 dice unless you spend Willpower, which negates the -5 but does not add +3 dice.&quot; With this wording, the Condition seems continue affecting the character for a scene after it resolves, which is a little awkward. Especially because the Devotion says the victim gains one Condition after the other resolves, and I doubt the intent is for the victim to suffer this penalty and the penalty from the Melancholic Condition simultaneously for one Scene. It's a minor tweak, but I think it would be a little cleaner to move &quot;Resolve this Condition&quot; to the end of the paragraph, and maybe add &quot;at the end of the Scene.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T18:14:02-08:00","id":1018631,"title":"","content":"I like the devotions overall, but I'm a bit disappointed by 2nd edition Sudden Strength. I know there are times when adding Celerity to Strength for a turn will be better than just using Physical Intensity, but it feels like those cases are the minority. Between the vitae cost, requiring an active effect of Celerity to be in effect, and the potential bashing damage, it just doesn't feel very rewarding.<br /> <br /> Then again, I didn't notice any other comments about it, so maybe it's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T19:01:13-08:00","id":1018643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jaerys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1018631#post1018631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the devotions overall, but I'm a bit disappointed by 2nd edition Sudden Strength. I know there are times when adding Celerity to Strength for a turn will be better than just using Physical Intensity, but it feels like those cases are the minority. Between the vitae cost, requiring an active effect of Celerity to be in effect, and the potential bashing damage, it just doesn't feel very rewarding.<br /> <br /> Then again, I didn't notice any other comments about it, so maybe it's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're activating both Celerity and Sudden Strength just for extra dice on a strength-based attack roll, then yeah, physical intensity is more efficient unless you have at least 4 dots of Celerity, and it's a wash at 4 dots. But, if you were already going to activate Celerity anyway, Sudden Strength is more efficient at only 3 dots. More importantly, Sudden Strength adds temporary Strength dots, whereas physical intensity only adds bonus dice. The increased Strength can be useful for other things, such as increasing the maximum Size of objects you can lift and throw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T21:20:15-08:00","id":1018679,"title":"","content":"I really think Aegis of Defiance should just be based off Clash of Wills, since 2e has been getting away from success comparisons, especially since it adds in the comparison to a power stat in the case of non-rolled stuff, which is just so much better served with CoW.<br /> <br /> That said, there's some cool stuff among there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T23:34:41-08:00","id":1018709,"title":"","content":"Violent Coercien should be Dominate or nightmare... not majesty...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T05:02:41-08:00","id":1018778,"title":"","content":"Sudden Strength is also cheap XP-wise, so its okay if its situational. Its not as simple as being better at Celeritt 3, though, because of the bashing damage you can tale for using it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T07:40:38-08:00","id":1018805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1018778#post1018778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sudden Strength is also cheap XP-wise, so its okay if its situational. Its not as simple as being better at Celeritt 3, though, because of the bashing damage you can tale for using it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more Vitae-efficient. That doesn't necessarily mean it's better. It's situational, like you said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T08:07:40-08:00","id":1018812,"title":"","content":"Just for clarification, do the 'Rapidity' and 'Slow but Steady' Devotions need to be purchased separately for each power they will affect, or will a single purchase affect all powers that fall within its particular dot-range?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T08:20:49-08:00","id":1018817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1018812#post1018812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for clarification, do the 'Rapidity' and 'Slow but Steady' Devotions need to be purchased separately for each power they will affect, or will a single purchase affect all powers that fall within its particular dot-range?</div> </div> </div> </div>They need to be purchased separately.<br /> <br /> What I want to know is if buying (for example) .22 Solid with Rapidity counts as a single Devotion that costs 2 Experiences, or two separate Devotions that cost 1 experience each. Because with Devotion Experimenter being a thing, that makes a big difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T09:10:59-08:00","id":1018826,"title":"","content":"The way I read Rapidity and Slow but Steady, they count as separate devotions so Devotion Experimenter doesn't reduce their cost if it would only be 1 experience normally. On the other hand, the devotion experimenter would gain a beat for both the base devotion and Rapidity if they taught a student both. This seems the most sensible interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1018805#post1018805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's more Vitae-efficient. That doesn't necessarily mean it's better. It's situational, like you said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, it's only more vitae efficient at Celerity 3 or 4 if your natural strength is low enough that you don't take bashing damage or don't count the vitae required to heal the damage. Counting the vitae needed to heal the potential bashing damage it is unlikely to be more vitae efficient for non-elders. To be fair, the healing can (hopefully) wait until after the fight so there are times when that trade off may be worthwhile. It still feels very situational.<br /> <br /> Using Sudden Strength to throw things could be fun, but it seems more like a parlor trick than a sound tactic. To pick up and throw a car (or similar sized object) would require an active effect from vigor as well, so you're already talking 3 vitae before spending anything on physical intensity or healing (4 if you want to add vigor to the weapon bonus). Even large, heavy thrown objects tend to only have a weapon damage bonus of 2-3 due to durability. To be fair though, if you throw a size 10+ object at a kindred it will do lethal damage. There are plenty of less vitae inefficient ways to go about inflicting non-bashing damage to kindred, but it has style, and you might find yourself in a situation where all you have to work with is a sedan.<br /> <br /> It's not so much that Sudden Strength has no uses as that it feels like they're situational enough that you're better off saving the experience unless you're an elder with a lot of Celerity and low natural strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 12-18-2016, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T10:12:19-08:00","id":1018840,"title":"","content":"The bonus speed is also potentially a big deal. Lets say you have Str 2, Dex 2, Vigor 2, Celerity 5 for a base speed of 11. You can move 66 yards reflexively or 132 with an action. Sudden Strength boosts that to 96 and 192.<br /> <br /> That may be useful in some situations?<br /> <br /> The hypothetical max speed goes from 138 / 276 to 168 / 336 yards instantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 12-18-2016, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T17:29:09-08:00","id":1018976,"title":"","content":"Aegis of Defiance is <i>nuts</i> when it comes to opposed rolls, especially for Ghouls (<i>can</i> Ghouls learn Devotions? I don't think the book says anything otherwise...)<br /> <br /> Replacing Attribute+BP with Attribute+Skill+Discipline is <i>good</i>, especially if you've got an appropriate Speciality.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> BFFs has a problem - Integrity doesn't rank Breaking Points by dots. So as it stands, there's no guide to what kind of penalty they'd take on their roll. You <i>might</i> want to take a look at that.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> .22 Solid and If You Can't Duck It are wonderful - and are <i>great</i> targets for Rapidity. In comparison, Sudden Strength and Hekireke are parlor tricks. Hekireke is the kind of thing that's <i>terrible</i> if you're in an actual fight, especially if the other side came prepared. Straight Up Fucking Murderer is pretty good, too - I haven't looked to see if it lets you do anything <i>really</i> crazy yet (it probably does).<br /> <br /> Bet yeah - .22 Solid, If You Can't Duck It, and Body of Will make you a <i>monster</i> in a fight. I want to get something straight, though - let's say I have .22 Solid active with Resilience 3, and someone hits me for 3 Aggravated. Would I end up taking 3 Bashing? Or do the two downgrades not stack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T17:51:34-08:00","id":1018981,"title":"","content":"Huh. RAW .22 Solid works vs sunlight. I am mot sure thats intended.<br /> <br /> Or I guess sunlight wouldnt be an &quot;attack&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T09:01:04-08:00","id":1019274,"title":"","content":"Hekireki lets you get bonus dice and vigor's effect without spending blood (instead you spend a willpower and an instant action). When you are trying to spend as little blood as possible that can be very useful. Its situational but, again, only 1xp. The charging effect is mostly pointless except maybe launching a surprise attack via obfuscate where you want to one shot someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T19:46:50-08:00","id":1019573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1019274#post1019274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hekireki lets you get bonus dice and vigor's effect without spending blood (instead you spend a willpower and an instant action). When you are trying to spend as little blood as possible that can be very useful. Its situational but, again, only 1xp. The charging effect is mostly pointless except maybe launching a surprise attack via obfuscate where you want to one shot someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but... unless you're real hard up for Vitae, losing an action is going to hurt a <i>lot</i> more in a real fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T20:24:39-08:00","id":1019583,"title":"","content":"Blood in a fight is life. Lets say you are BP 1 eith some celerity and vigor. If you spend blood on attacking, you can't use Celerity's autododge. With this you can do both, and on the next turn you celerity surprise + attack with a hopefully debilitating blow.<br /> <br /> In situations where you cant feed on your opponent or convenient food stock you need to conserve blood as well.<br /> <br /> Body of Will also combines nicely with it. If you dont have yo spend vitae on vigor, you can basically double the damage bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 12-20-2016, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T22:25:15-08:00","id":1019618,"title":"","content":"Except you <i>can't</i> use the Celerity auto-dodge on the charge-up turn - you aren't allowed to spend Vitae that turn (2nd sentence of the Devotion's effect). Which leaves you <i>kinda screwed</i>, since your opponent can just kick your shit in while you're getting ready. And let's hope your opponent didn't bring buddies along, because you're only going to be able to hit one of them!<br /> <br /> Basically, the Devotion makes you waste a turn, potentially damages you, and lets you super-attack <i>one person</i> - who might, you know, just <i>auto-dodge the attack with Celerity</i>.Meanwhile, the guy who spenf the 2xp Ol' Heki costs (not 1xp - I checked) on a more <i>useful</i> Devotion (like If You Can't Duck It) is laughing in your face. Because they have something <i>broadly</i> useful, and you have something that... isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 12-20-2016, 01:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T23:46:43-08:00","id":1019636,"title":"","content":"It's good for sneak attacks. It doesn't really need to be good for more than that, cause that's what you (should) get it for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T00:11:26-08:00","id":1019641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1019618#post1019618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except you <i>can't</i> use the Celerity auto-dodge on the charge-up turn - you aren't allowed to spend Vitae that turn (2nd sentence of the Devotion's effect). Which leaves you <i>kinda screwed</i>, since your opponent can just kick your shit in while you're getting ready. And let's hope your opponent didn't bring buddies along, because you're only going to be able to hit one of them!<br /> <br /> Basically, the Devotion makes you waste a turn, potentially damages you, and lets you super-attack <i>one person</i> - who might, you know, just <i>auto-dodge the attack with Celerity</i>.Meanwhile, the guy who spenf the 2xp Ol' Heki costs (not 1xp - I checked) on a more <i>useful</i> Devotion (like If You Can't Duck It) is laughing in your face. Because they have something <i>broadly</i> useful, and you have something that... isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all assuming you're using it during an already active, ongoing fight, when people are aware of you. If you are, then you at least have Celerity available to defend yourself. &quot;<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Consolas\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">She may use Vitae for Celerity during this time, but it does not add to the total used on the Devotion.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Also, it's really nice if you're trying to jam a stake into someone to both start and finish the conflict.<br /> <br /> I've also seen it used to absolutely devastating effect when a relatively non-combat capable coterie was acting as a group to distract a monstrous elder they struggled to even harm. It turned the tables from minor scratches and misses every turn into a one-shot kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 12-20-2016, 05:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T02:43:18-08:00","id":1019671,"title":"","content":"The devotion gives an exception for celerity. You can use it.<br /> <br /> Now, Straight Up Fucking Murderer. All-Out Attack is +3 Dice, which is better than just spending 1v normally. Thrust from Light Weapon Style seems like the best use of the talent--turning your Defense into bonus dice with no downside for 1v.<br /> <br /> Improvised Weapon 3 is another winner with it, especially if you have used You Cant Duck This on that item to give it a lot of structure.<br /> <br /> Combine the two, with an improvised piece of wood, targeting the heart.<br /> <br /> Chain Weapons 1 lets you sacrifice your defense to cause 2B to everyone who attacks you.<br /> <br /> Light Weapons 5 lets you inflict +1 Agg, which is very situational but useful in those situations (e.g. vs werewolf no silver and cant run).<br /> <br /> Cant think of too many other great uses for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 12-20-2016, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T08:43:37-08:00","id":1019791,"title":"","content":"I'm in love with Natural Born Killer. It combines two of my favorite Carthian Devotions in 1e (Guardian Vigil and Hair Trigger) and makes the latter much more fair by limiting its use to the first turn. Not that you'll usually need it after that anyway. With a Crossbow you're guaranteed to stake on a hit. This gets even stronger with Hurt Locker's ammo capacity rules, allowing you to use burst fire. Throw in Trigger Discipline so you can do a Medium burst to hit up to three targets and Powered Projectile to reduce the penalty for targeting the heart. Absolutely beautiful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T10:19:46-08:00","id":1019832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1019671#post1019671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The devotion gives an exception for celerity. You can use it.<br /> <br /> Now, Straight Up Fucking Murderer. All-Out Attack is +3 Dice, which is better than just spending 1v normally. Thrust from Light Weapon Style seems like the best use of the talent--turning your Defense into bonus dice with no downside for 1v.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way Hekireki is written it seems you can't spend vitae on Celerity during the initial turn, only on the following turns. If that's not the intent then the wording needs to be tweaked a bit. I actually like Hekireki well enough. It's a risky technique, but it has its uses, and it does strike me as a good devotion to activate <i>before</i> starting a fight.<br /> <br /> I wonder if Straight Up Fucking Murder is supposed to work for the Thrust Maneuver (Light Weapons 2). That does &quot;sacrifice Defense&quot;, but it's doing so on a one for one basis rather than an all or nothing trade off.<br /> <br /> PS - This a minor point, but All-Out Attack is only a +2 Dice modifier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 12-20-2016, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T04:53:19-08:00","id":1020825,"title":"","content":"If You Can't Duck It<br /> <br /> So, anyone who has played Exalted knows how powerful scenelong dice adders are. This devotion plus Loght Weapons 2 lets you add your Celerity to your dicepool twice. Hekireki makes for three times. This devotion makes me wonder whether or not spamming Celerity is a viable combat build now.<br /> <br /> Also of note that you can combine the resilience aspect with the improvised weapon style 2 and 3 to a horrible conclusion--even better when combined with Rapidity.<br /> <br /> That makes it an on-tap (Resilience *2) bonus Health Levels and lets you convert half of that into bonus damage.<br /> <br /> The Vigor part is notable when using a normal improvised weapon (particularly with the thrown aspect of Vigor) since it directly buffs damage.<br /> <br /> Other uses include making something exceptionally durable.<br /> <br /> Strangely, RAW, dice bonus works on, e.g. computers or textbooks, even though that makes no sense with the fluff. Then again neither does a rope adding to climbing more. So... magic?<br /> <br /> Overall, if I plan on investing heavily into the physical disciplines I would always pick up this Devotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T04:55:17-08:00","id":1024714,"title":"","content":"I know it's a minor thing but it gets under my skin - Sudden Strength's formula for Force is mixed up with Kinetic Energy. Force is Mass by Acceleration (rate of change of velocity). Kinetic Energy is half Mass by Velocity squared.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T20:26:50-08:00","id":1026293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1020825#post1020825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, anyone who has played Exalted knows how powerful scenelong dice adders are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted is a wildly different game, with wildly different expectations for numbers of dice rolls in a given scene. It's a bad comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T20:58:07-08:00","id":1026842,"title":"","content":"Random question (I asked it earlier but I don't think I actually got an answer):<br /> <br /> If I have Resistance \u2022\u2022\u2022 and have .22 Solid active, can I downgrade up to 3 levels of non-sunlight Aggravated damage to Bashing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T21:31:10-08:00","id":1026851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1026842#post1026842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random question (I asked it earlier but I don't think I actually got an answer):<br /> <br /> If I have Resistance \u2022\u2022\u2022 and have .22 Solid active, can I downgrade up to 3 levels of non-sunlight Aggravated damage to Bashing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <br /> <br /> Editing to effect: <br /> <br /> .22 Solid<br /> (Protean \u2022\u2022, Resilience \u2022)<br /> This Devotion hardens the user's flesh, and coagulates the blood in such a way as to act as &quot;internal armor&quot;. While few things cause lasting harm to Kindred, this Devotion takes things a step further, and makes almost everything a vampire suffers as bad as a bruise. <br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Instant<br /> For the remainder of the scene, every attack which would cause your character lethal damage is lessened by this Devotion. Downgrade a number of lethal damage from each such attack equal to your character's Resilience dots. For example, if your character with Resilience \u2022\u2022\u2022 suffers three attacks in a turn, one for one lethal damage, one for three lethal damage, and one for five lethal damage, your character would ultimately suffer two lethal damage and seven bashing damage. <br /> Note that this is in addition to Resilience's normal downgrading effect. Aggravated damage reduced to lethal by Resilience can be further downgraded by .22 Solid to bashing damage. So, for example, if a vampire with Resilience \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 and .22 Solid took a strike causing seven aggravated damage, if she activated .22 Solid, she'd take 3 aggravated damage and four bashing damage.<br /> This Devotion costs 1 Experience to learn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:23:01-08:00","id":1027043,"title":"","content":"I'd love if Onyx Path would release a Devotion creation Guide, pointing out what Disciplines should be used for what and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:37:21-08:00","id":1027053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1016390-secrets-of-the-covenants-hidden-devotions?p=1027043#post1027043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love if Onyx Path would release a Devotion creation Guide, pointing out what Disciplines should be used for what and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it's first edition, the advice in Danse Macabre still works very well for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate